        "raw": "<p>I&#39;m running the quickstart issues and next session we&#39;ll be tackling&nbsp;<em>Tome of The Bizarre #86</em>. I&#39;ve readthe adventure and there are some details I want to change, but there&#39;s two major ones:</p><p>-I want the events to be set on the&nbsp;<strong>real</strong> Tomb of Anubis.&nbsp;</p><p>-But it&#39;s still connected to Baron Blade&#39;s plans to distract the heroes (while gathering forces for issue 6).&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>So instead of robots and Miss Information&#39;s traps the characters will be facing real mummies and genuine dangers from the temple, but my problem is how to fit it in the major plot. Here are some ideas I&#39;&#39;m playing with:&nbsp;</p><p>-Baron Blade found a way to open a portal to the temple in New Vegas, risking letting out all the monsters and dark energies into the city if the players can&#39;t close it from the other side (there would be a machine inside the temple keeping the passage open, serving as a clue to Baron&#39;s identity). The new Anubis went to investigate the portal but got captured by the temple&#39;s traps.&nbsp;</p><p>-Miss Information, hired by Baron Blade, used her powers to open the New Vegas portal as a way to lure the heroes in and let the Temple itself deal with them. Maybe she planned to capture Anubis to serve as bait.&nbsp;</p><p>-Blade made a deal with Ammit? Maybe he gave her the new Anubis in exchange for dealing with the heroes, but I&#39;m not sure if it would make sense for both to interact this way.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Anyways, what are your thoughts?&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
