        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/ad7895/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2018-09-05T17:41:14.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Ah, I see. That does make sense. However it raises a bit of a potential problem, as I see it with Anubis' own presence there, as having him fall prey to the traps and dangers of what is, essentially, his own home would be a bit... well, odd. So it would probably be better to go where a version where Anubis was, somehow, captured independently by Blade or Miss Information (or someone else) and then imprisoned by external forces within the tomb itself?</p><p>Perhaps the generator you suggested initially is actually powered by the energy of the captured Anubis, which would explain why Blade found it necessary not only to capture him, but also to keep him there in the first place?</p>",
